Package: retrobox-core
Replaces: retrobox
Conflicts: retrobox
Version: @VERSION@
Section: games
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Manu Romero <manu4.2012@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/RetroboxProject/retrobox-core
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: retrobox-emulationstation, retrobox-mangohud, python3-gamepadly, @RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: kscreen
Description: Retrobox core: batocera-style backend for a Linux desktop
 Port of the batocera backend stack (batocera-configgen) to a standard
 Linux desktop. Writes emulator configuration automatically on game launch
 and handles bezels, shaders and gamepad auto-configuration, to be used
 with a compiled batocera-emulationstation frontend.
 .
 This package installs the project under /opt/retrobox (read-only) and an
 optional system-wide configuration layer in /etc/retrobox. User data
 (ROMs, saves, BIOS) lives in ~/.local/share/retrobox and user settings in
 ~/.config/retrobox, never in /opt/retrobox.
 .
 The EmulationStation frontend (retrobox-emulationstation), the patched
 MangoHud build (retrobox-mangohud), the pad-to-keyboard mapper (python3-gamepadly) and the emulators are separate packages.
